### Smalltalk01

smalltalk01-line1-a = Fair weather today, wouldn't you say?
smalltalk01-line1-b = Aye, a fine day. May it stay this calm till dusk.

smalltalk01-line2-a = Have you heard any news from the nearby villages?
smalltalk01-line2-b = Only rumors, friend. But rumors keep the world turning.

### Smalltalk02

smalltalk02-line1-a = Greetings. Roads seem quieter than usual.
smalltalk02-line1-b = Quiet roads are a blessing. Means fewer troubles wandering about.

smalltalk02-line2-a = Any advice for a traveler passing through?
smalltalk02-line2-b = Keep your purse close, your boots dry, and never ignore a warm hearth.

smalltalk02-line3-a = Sounds like wisdom earned the hard way.
smalltalk02-line3-b = In these lands, that's the only way wisdom comes.
